108:def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
109:    """
110:    Extend the solid 3x3 square into clipped red diagonal corner rays and yellow side-center ribbons.
111:
112:    Input structure
113:    - The background is the dominant color.
114:    - The input has exactly two foreground colors: one forms a solid 3x3 square, and the other forms scattered blocker pixels.
115:    - The 3x3 square is the source; all original foreground pixels remain unchanged.
116:
117:    Rule
118:    - Paint red one-cell diagonal rays outward from the four square corners until a blocker, edge, or row-wise foreground pinch stops the ray.
119:    - Paint yellow diagonal ribbons from the top, left, bottom, and right side centers in a clockwise pinwheel: NE, NW, SW, and SE.
120:    - A yellow ribbon alternates a single center cell with a three-cell horizontal or vertical slice; a blocker encountered within a slice stops the ribbon after any earlier cells in that slice are painted.
121:
122:    Key insight
123:    - The square defines four corner rays and four side-center ribbons, while the scattered foreground pixels are not targets; they are blockers that clip these local diagonal extrusions.
124:    """
125:    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
